"""Reporting rationale checked on 23 October; never used to select a model."""


def add_metric_rationale(add, page, table):
    page()
    add('## Evaluation choices and the literature')
    add('I checked the original YOLOv7 and ISIC 2018 challenge papers, together with the evaluator used in this project. The Project 3 specification names YOLOv7 or newer but does not prescribe one paper or a formula for averaging box IoU. These sources guide the reporting choices below; their benchmark scores are not directly comparable with this two-class subset.')
    add('YOLOv7 [4, Section 5.1 and Table 2] uses COCO training, validation and test sets, and reports AP, AP50, AP75, object-size AP and FPS. This supports reporting detection quality across overlap thresholds alongside computing cost. Its table does not define the all-GT or TP-only mean box IoU used here. The present model is Ultralytics YOLOv8, so [3] is the implementation reference.')
    add('The ISIC 2018 challenge paper [6, Sections 2.1 and 2.3] uses thresholded pixel-mask Jaccard for Task 1: mask overlap below 0.65 contributes zero. Task 3 uses balanced accuracy, the mean class recall, for seven disease classes. This supports examining class imbalance, but neither task is this binary box detector. I do not transfer the mask threshold or equate pixel-mask Jaccard with bounding-box IoU.')
    add('### What each result adds')
    table(['Measure retained', 'Reason and limit'], [
        ['AP50 and AP50:95, overall and per class', 'Summarize score-ranked detection over permissive and stricter overlap thresholds. Per-class AP exposes the malignant weakness hidden by the mean. AP does not give recall at the chosen operating threshold.'],
        ['Fixed-threshold detection precision, recall and F1', 'Describe the retained boxes: missed lesions, false detections and their balance. F1 weights precision and recall equally; it does not encode clinical costs.'],
        ['Image Accuracy, class recall/F1 and coverage', 'Check the diagnosis attached to the primary prediction, including abstentions. Class recall and macro F1 prevent the larger benign group from dominating the account. Omitting them would hide asymmetric errors.'],
        ['All-GT and TP-only box IoU', 'Separate overlap across the cohort from overlap conditional on successful detection. Class-agnostic values help identify class errors; correct-class values also reflect recognition failures. These custom averages complement detection metrics.'],
        ['Primary-box IoU and image alerts', 'The highest-score box can be chosen without GT, unlike a best-overlap diagnostic. Any malignant box can raise an alert even if the primary class is benign. Alerts show this extra burden, not biopsy counts.'],
    ])
    add('The following definitions and interpretations are reporting additions made after development. They do not replace the original validation selection rule. This literature check did not trigger training, inference, a new threshold scan or model selection. Source locations and checks are recorded in `evaluation_sources_20261023.json`.')

    page()
    add('## Exact metric definitions and implementation limits')
    add('### Detection and AP')
    add('At the fixed operating point, precision = TP/(TP+FP), recall = TP/(TP+FN), and F1 = 2TP/(2TP+FP+FN). Predictions are processed in descending confidence; a TP needs the correct class and IoU >= 0.5 with the still-unmatched GT. Every extra box is FP. This study has one GT lesion per image. No finite set of background boxes is defined, so box-level TN and detection accuracy are not reported.')
    add('AP uses the pinned Ultralytics evaluator [3]: class-correct IoU matching, score-ranked precision-recall curves, and 101-point interpolated trapezoidal integration. AP50 uses IoU 0.50; AP50:95 averages ten cutoffs from 0.50 to 0.95 in steps of 0.05. mAP averages the two classes equally. The AP floor is 0.001, not the operational 0.40 threshold. AP uses upstream `match_predictions` at each cutoff, while our fixed-point counts use a separate confidence-ordered matcher. The fixed-point counts should not be read from the library\'s max-F1 summary.')
    add('We retain single-label, class-aware NMS at 0.70 and max_det=300. Official COCO evaluation [7] uses its own matching and accumulation, with standard maxDets=100 and 101 recall points. Our AP values follow the COCO-style IoU range but are not a reproduction of the official COCO benchmark. AP was not independently recomputed; the separate count and IoU audits do not validate its numerical implementation.')
    add('### Image classification and averaging')
    add('The primary class comes from the highest-confidence retained box, without GT-based selection or an IoU test. No box is an abstention: it contributes an incorrect image label and a FN for its true class. Accuracy divides correct image labels by all 165 images. Coverage divides images with a prediction by 165; conditional accuracy divides correct labels by covered images. Class recall divides correct labels in that class by its GT count. This is the classwise correct fraction reported here, rather than a one-versus-rest accuracy inflated by other-class TN. Macro F1 averages the two class F1 values; balanced accuracy averages their recalls.')
    add('### Box overlap and its denominator')
    add('IoU = intersection area / union area for two axis-aligned boxes. For each GT, the all-GT diagnostic takes the largest retained-box IoU under the stated class rule, or zero if no eligible box exists. A correct-class box below IoU 0.5 still contributes its actual overlap, even though it is a detection FN. Thus "all GT" does not mean every detection FN is forcibly zero. Requiring the correct class makes this a joint recognition/overlap diagnostic, not a pure measure of geometry.')
    add('TP-only averages the boxes matched by the fixed-threshold detector and excludes unmatched GTs. Primary-box IoU uses the highest-score box; it is zero for no prediction and, in the correct-class variant, for a wrong primary class. Best-overlap diagnostics use GT to choose a box and do not penalize duplicates, so they must accompany precision and recall. Overall IoU pools the per-lesion values; per-class means use GT diagnosis, even when predicted class is ignored. For all-GT measures N=165 overall, 124 benign and 41 malignant. TP-only denominators are the corresponding TP counts. These are project-defined summaries, not the ISIC mask metric or a prescribed YOLO paper metric.')
